  <main>
    <div class="left-column"></div>
    <div class="center-column">
      <h1>Michael Heilmann's Arcadia ADL</h1>
      <p>
      ADL, the Arcadia asset definition language, is the format in which the assets
      of Michael Heilmann's Arcadia are stored. An ADL asset is a description of a
      definition: a color, a material, a mesh, a model, a texture, a pixel buffer,
      a sample buffer, or one of several other kinds. Applications load ADL assets
      at runtime, resolve the references between them, and feed the resulting
      definitions to the Arcadia engine.
      </p>

      <h2>Documentation</h2>
